'''Arıca''' ({{langx|ku|Kefri}};{{sfnp|Biner|2020|p=x}}{{efn|Also spelt as Kafri, Kefrê, or Kefré.{{sfnmp|Tan|2018|1p=172|2a1=Jongerden|2a2=Verheij|2y=2012|2p=321|Gaunt|2006|3p=231}}}} {{langx|syr|Kafro Elayto}}){{sfnp|Biner|2020|p=x}}{{efn|Alternatively transliterated as Käfro ʿēläito, Kafro Eleito, Kafro Eloyto, or Kefro Elayto.{{sfnmp|Sinclair|1989|1p=319|Tamcke|2012|2p=18|Keser Kayaalp|2021|3p=163|Ritter|1967|4p=11}} Also known as Kafrah Tāğdū.{{sfnp|Bcheiry|2009|p=52}} Also called Upper Kafra or Upper Kafro or simply Kafra, in contrast with Lower Kafro ([[Elbeğendi, Midyat|Kafro Tahtayo]]).{{sfnmp|Barsoum|2008|1pp=18, 30|Gaunt|2006|2pp=231, 232|Palmer|1990|3p=xx}} [[Nisba (onomastics)|Nisba]]: Käfrōyo.{{sfnp|Ritter|1967|p=11}}}} is a village in the district of [[Gercüş]], [[Batman Province]] in [[Turkey]]. It is populated by [[Assyrian people|Syriacs]] and by [[Kurds]] of the [[Kurdish tribes|Kercoz tribe]].{{sfnp|Tan|2018|p=172}} In 2021, the population was 344.<ref>{{Cite web |title=Address-based population registration system (ADNKS) results dated 31 December 2021 |url=https://www.tuik.gov.tr/indir/duyuru/favori_raporlar.xlsx |access-date=12 January 2023 |publisher=[[TÜİK]] |language=tr |format=XLS}}</ref> It is located in the historic region of [[Tur Abdin]].{{sfnp|Barsoum|2008|p=15}}

In the village, there are churches of [[Mar (title)|Mor]] Aho and Mor Dimet, Mor Ya’qub, and of Mor Barsaumo.{{sfnmp|Sinclair|1989|1p=319|Barsoum|2008|2p=18}}<ref>{{cite web |url=https://www.soc-wus.org/westernarchdiocese/news%20destroyed%20monasteries%20&%20churches.htm|title=Threatened or destroy

