The '''1st Missouri Field Battery''' was a [[Field artillery in the American Civil War|field artillery]] [[artillery battery|battery]] that served in the [[Confederate States Army]] during the [[American Civil War]]. The battery was formed by [[Captain (United States O-3)|Captain]] Westley F. Roberts in [[Arkansas]] in September 1862 as '''Roberts' Missouri Battery''' and was originally armed with two [[James rifle|12-pounder James rifles]] and two [[M1841 6-pounder field gun|6-pounder smoothbore guns]]. The unit fought in the [[Battle of Prairie Grove]] on December 7, as part of a Confederate offensive. Roberts' Battery withdrew after the battle and transferred to [[Little Rock, Arkansas]], where Roberts resigned and was replaced by [[Lieutenant]] Samuel T. Ruffner.

