'''''3 of Hearts''''' is the debut [[studio album]] by American girl group [[3 of Hearts]]. It was released on July 24, 2001, through the [[record label]] [[RCA Records Nashville|RCA Nashville]]. ''3 of Hearts'' is a [[teen pop]] and [[country music]] album, though according to some music critics, it leans more towards [[pop music]]. The album was managed by American producer [[Byron Gallimore]]; its marketing focused on the group's [[Crossover music|crossover appeal]] to target a teenaged and young-adult audience. 3 of Hearts performed on two national tours sponsored by [[Seventeen (American magazine)|''Seventeen'']] magazine and [[Walmart]] respectively, and the singers were featured in several marketing campaigns.

